Accepted by the main session, 2026-08-10.

NewIngester, Run and SkippedNullKeys measure 0% because their only honest
exercise needs a real broker: Run's contract (partition discovery, resume
at checkpoint+1, poll/apply loop) is exactly what the roadmap's verification
criterion tests via the integration suite, which is build-tagged
(-tags integration) and therefore invisible to the unit coverage run.

That suite is step 2 of the frozen plan rpkv-01-ingest (file
ingest/ingester_integration_test.go, commit "test(ingest): crash-restart
convergence against the dev loop") and lands on this same branch before
anything is pushed. Faking unit coverage of Run with a mocked kgo client
would test the mock, not the contract, and contradict the black-box
contract-test discipline in CLAUDE.md.

resumeOffset and collectEntries - the logic that can be unit-tested - are
at 100%.
